        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions — Neelam / Blue Sapphire</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Does Blue Sapphire change colour over time? No. Natural and properly heat-treated Blue Sapphires are colour-stable for life. A sudden visible change almost always points to unstable treatment — not the stone itself.</li>
          <li>Are Blue Sapphires treated? Most are either untreated or heat-treated. Both are acceptable when disclosed. We do not carry glass-filled or diffusion-treated stones under any circumstances.</li>
          <li>Can Neelam be worn daily? Yes. At Mohs 9, Blue Sapphire is exceptionally durable and well-suited to daily wear when securely set.</li>
          <li>Which metal pairs best with Blue Sapphire? Silver or Panchdhatu traditionally. White Gold may be used when astrologically advised.</li>
          <li>How soon do the effects of Blue Sapphire appear? Typically within 3–8 weeks, provided the stone is suited to the wearer's horoscope. Effects are gradual and cumulative — not sudden.</li>
          <li>What is the ideal weight for astrological use? 2–7 carats, guided by the horoscope and the strength of Saturn's placement.</li>
          <li>Can Blue Sapphire be worn during Sadhe Saati? Yes — but only when Saturn is favourable in the chart and after proper astrological testing or guidance. Do not wear it on assumption alone. Sadhe Saati affects everyone differently, and the stone must match the individual, not the transit.</li>
          <li>Is a flawless Blue Sapphire always better? No. Natural Blue Sapphires typically contain inclusions. A stone with balanced colour, fine natural silk, and structural stability is far more valuable than one that looks unnaturally perfect. Perfection in a sapphire is often a reason to look closer, not pay more.</li>
          <li>How is Neelam different from other Saturn stones? Blue Sapphire (Neelam) is the primary gemstone of Saturn and the strongest among Shani ratnas. It works directly on Saturn's energy in the chart — unlike substitute stones, which work more gently. This is why expert consultation before wearing is essential.</li>
        </ul>
