    {%- when 'turquoise' -%}
      <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--turquoise">
        <p>Frequently Asked Questions</p>
        <p>What makes Turquoise different from other gemstones in this collection? Turquoise is a porous, organic-feeling stone with a sensitivity to moisture, oils, and chemicals that crystalline gems do not share. This makes it more care-intensive, but also gives it a warmth and character that polished stones often lack.</p>
        <p>Is stabilised Turquoise suitable for astrological use? High-quality stabilised Turquoise is generally accepted when disclosed. Natural, untreated stones are preferred where available and within budget.</p>
        <p>Can Turquoise change colour over time? Yes — if it absorbs sweat, oils, or chemicals it can darken permanently. Consistent care after every wear is the most effective prevention.</p>
        <p>Which origin is better — Iranian or American? Iranian Turquoise is the traditional benchmark for astrological use, valued for its fine texture and classic colour. American Turquoise offers striking character and is well regarded for jewellery. For astrological purposes, Iranian origin is generally preferred when accessible.</p>
